# Session log discipline (`docs/SESSIONS.md`)

Cursor-side mirror of the Claude Code `warn-session-log` stop hook
(`.claude/hookify.session-log.local.md`). This repo runs from several concurrent
Cursor **and** Claude Code worktrees with no chronological timeline otherwise, so a
missed entry makes a session unresumable and hides parallel-session collisions.

> **Incident this closes:** the 2026-07-12 four-firms prop-portfolio ADR
> (`docs/adr/2026-07-12-prop-portfolio-four-friendly-firms.md`, recorded by a Cursor
> Cloud Agent) landed on `main` with **no** SESSIONS entry — there was no Cursor-side
> session-log rule at the time.

## When to write

At **session wrap-up**, write a full entry only for a real judgment call: a choice
among options, a scope/priority/risk decision, or a measurement that resolves an
open question. Follow the living `docs/SESSIONS.md` header; entries are reverse
chronological (**newest on top**).

Mechanical output without a judgment call, trivial turns and read-only turns need
no full entry, even if a commit shipped. The A–D classes/~40-word targets are retired.

## Entry shape (append-only; link out, never restate canonical values)

- **Focus** — what the session set out to do
- **Shipped** — branch + commit + concrete deltas (link artifacts, don't duplicate)
- **Decisions/defects** — link the actual decision owner (specification, campaign,
  plan, PR, existing ADR, notice or brief as applicable)
- **Open / next** — optional context specific to that historical session. Do not
  copy the current queue into an entry or add a stub solely because the queue changed.
- **Live-ops state** — lock / allocation / gate status where relevant

The living header in `docs/SESSIONS.md` links to the `STATE.md` operator queue, which
owns current priorities and obligations. Canonical owner: `docs/operational_rules.md
§7`. Do **not** restate risk %, MC anchor, strategy versions, or hashes — link to their
owners (`CLAUDE.md`, `docs/adr/`, `LOCK.md`). User rules override this file.
